    "NYC": {
      "publisher": "Port Authority of New York and New Jersey (PANYNJ), Airport Noise and Operations Management System",
      "report": "Monthly Noise Monitor Report for JFK, LGA, EWR and TEB, June 2026 and July 2026 editions",
      "url": "https://www.panynj.gov/content/dam/port-authority/aircraft-noise/panynj-noise-monitoring-jul-2026.pdf",
      "licence": "a public report; no licence stated. Used as published facts with the source named; no images or tables are redistributed",
      "metric": "monthly aircraft DNL. DNL has no evening penalty, so it could read quieter than Lden; measured from the hour of every July-August 2026 movement (scripts/measure_dnl_lden_gap.py), Lden - DNL is JFK +0.01, LGA +0.13, EWR +0.06, TEB +0.27 dB, stored as lden_minus_dnl and added before any comparison",
      "lden_minus_dnl": {
        "JFK": 0.01,
        "LGA": 0.13,
        "EWR": 0.06,
        "TEB": 0.27
      },
      "method_change": "from January 2026 the readings use ANEEM, which captures quieter aircraft events: at loud sites it barely moves the figure, at quiet ones it reads several dB higher (EWR E29_P 36-43 dB to 48-50; at SFO, where both are published all year, ANEEM - conventional is median +0.19 dB at sites over 55 dB and +2.59 below, up to +9.5). dnl_year mixes six months of each; dnl_aneem is January-July 2026 alone",
      "period_year": [
        "2025-07-01",
        "2026-06-30"
      ],
      "period_aneem": [
        "2026-01-01",
        "2026-07-31"
      ],
      "transcription": "tables are images: read from the July and June editions separately and compared, 384 overlapping cells, 0 differ (scripts/panynj_monthly_dnl.py is the record)",
      "positions_from": "the report maps place a pin only roughly, so each monitor is the nearest point on the street its site table names to its map pin (scripts/snap_panynj_monitors.py, OpenStreetMap geometry); snap_m is how far the pin was from that street; pin_lat/pin_lon is the map-derived pin (scripts/georef_panynj_monitors.py: pins detected, maps calibrated symmetrically on the FAA runway thresholds at three colour thresholds; position_spread_m is how far a pin moves between those calibrations). street_verified false or null: the street was not confirmed, and the monitor is left out of any fit",
      "not_used": [
        {
          "id": "KEWHI",
          "why": "on the map, absent from the monthly table"
        },
        {
          "id": "RMS06",
          "why": "on the map, absent from the monthly table"
        },
        {
          "id": "LFOXST",
          "why": "in the LGA table from December 2025 only; on no map or site list, so no position (not transcribed)"
        }
      ],
